@reactions tradition
// W3, rec deck: the day after each rec tradition (social's cue tradition.<id>, one day), past tense; .you to someone
// who came. The ids are the proposed rec ids (content/trad-words/*.words; RA confirms).

? cue:tradition.winner-stays-on !cue:tradition.winner-stays-on.you
- Pell stayed on the court for three hours yesterday. He ate lunch between points.   #funny
- Winner Stays On was packed. The stands were louder than the mess at dinner.
? cue:tradition.winner-stays-on.you tier>=acquaintance
- Saw you on the court yesterday! You've got a proper backhand coming.
- You put your name on Pell's board. Brave. He rubs out the brave ones first.   #funny

? cue:tradition.lightdisc-cup !cue:tradition.lightdisc-cup.you
- That Cup final! I shouted so much I've got no voice left.   #funny
- The Cup board has a new name. My department's furious. In a nice way.
? cue:tradition.lightdisc-cup.you tier>=acquaintance
- You played in the Cup! How far did you get? Doesn't matter. You played.   #warm

? cue:tradition.dawn-swim.you tier>=acquaintance
- You came to dawn swim! Rina noticed. She said "Hm." That's good, from Rina.   #funny
- Early swim yesterday? You looked very awake at breakfast. Suspiciously awake.   #funny

? cue:tradition.paddle-club !cue:tradition.paddle-club.you
- Holt took paddle club round the loop twice. Nobody fell in. He looked almost pleased.
? cue:tradition.paddle-club.you tier>=acquaintance
- Holt says you held your paddle properly at paddle club. He told me. Unprompted.   #warm

? cue:tradition.river-regatta !cue:tradition.river-regatta.you
- Who got the pennant? I was cheering from the concourse glass. Couldn't see a thing.   #funny
- The regatta horn went off under the officers' corridor. Vance says he wasn't startled.   #funny
? cue:tradition.river-regatta.you tier>=acquaintance
- You paddled the fun heat! You went round the bend sideways. It looked brilliant.   #funny

? cue:tradition.wall-night !cue:tradition.wall-night.you
- Wall night was busy. The bell rang so often Tomas stopped counting. Vance didn't.   #funny
? cue:tradition.wall-night.you tier>=acquaintance
- I heard you rang the bell on Wall night! Your name's on the board now.   #warm
- My arms are still dead from Wall night. Are yours? Tell me yours are.   #funny

? cue:tradition.float-hour.you tier>=acquaintance
- Did you sleep well after float hour? I slept like a stone. A floating stone.   #funny
- Float hour was lovely, wasn't it? Nobody said a word. Not one.   #warm

? cue:tradition.slow-stretch.you tier>=acquaintance
- You came to slow stretch. How's your back? Mine's never been better.

? cue:tradition.rec-talent-night !cue:tradition.rec-talent-night.you
- Talent night was brilliant. The duet! And the spanner juggling. Mostly the spanners.   #funny
- Lucia's a born host. She made every act sound like the best thing aboard.   #warm
? cue:tradition.rec-talent-night.you tier>=acquaintance
- You did an act at talent night! People are still talking about it.   #warm
- Your act! I clapped till my hands hurt. Do another one next time.   #warm
- I saw you at talent night. You were braver than me. I just clapped.

? cue:tradition.all-hands !cue:tradition.all-hands.you
- Did you hear the Captain at the all-hands? Short, kind, then dinner. Perfect.
? cue:tradition.all-hands.you tier>=acquaintance
- Good to see you at the all-hands. The Captain looks round the room. She noticed.   #warm

? cue:tradition.wren-talk !cue:tradition.wren-talk.you
- Good Wren talk last night. I learned a thing. I've already forgotten it, but I learned it.   #funny
? cue:tradition.wren-talk.you tier>=acquaintance
- You were at the talk last night! Did you ask anything? I always think of mine after.
